From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Double-tap to wake switch in Settings > Display

The Zinwa Q25 touch panel can wake the screen on a double tap once the
touch driver arms its wakeup gesture (kernel patch 0903). Settings >
Display gets a Double-tap to wake switch after Screen timeout. Settings
only stores the choice in persist.sys.sable.dt2w (1 or 0); init copies
it to the driver's wake_gesture module parameter (sable-dt2w.rc). Shown
only where the product sets ro.sable.double_tap_wake. Off by default.
---
 res/values/sable_dt2w_strings.xml             | 23 +++++++
 res/xml/display_settings.xml                  |  9 +++
 ...ableDoubleTapWakePreferenceController.java | 65 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 97 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 res/values/sable_dt2w_strings.xml
 create mode 100644 src/com/android/settings/sable/SableDoubleTapWakePreferenceController.java

